<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Eblani</h1><p class="st-meta">100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of eastern Ireland named in Ptolemy's Geography, whose town Eblana has often, though doubtfully, been linked with Dublin.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Eblani are known only from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geography-ptolemy">Geography of Ptolemy</a>, compiled around 150 from earlier sailors' reports. He places them on the east coast of Ireland, south of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/voluntii">Voluntii</a> and north of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cauci">Cauci</a>, roughly in the area of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-dublin">County Dublin</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-mide">Meath</a>, with a town called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eblana">Eblana</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is recorded of their rulers, society or customs. The resemblance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eblana">Eblana</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> led older writers to identify the two, but most scholars now doubt the link, since Dublin's name is Irish and Ptolemy's coordinates are imprecise. Archaeology shows Roman goods reaching the east coast at sites such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drumanagh">Drumanagh</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Eblani do not appear in any later source, and no Irish tradition preserves their name. Their area later fell within the territory of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Kingdom of Leinster</a> and of the rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> dynasties of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-brega">Brega</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:61.69%;width:1.99%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Goidelic Celtic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Eblanii</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=eblani" aria-label="Eblani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4499 337 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Eblani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4819 593h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4819 593h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ireland. <a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=eblani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

